Product-specific terms (order terms in the sense of Section 2)

1. Evaluation. The designers run for ninety days from the first form opened. After that a
   designer requires a licence. The editor, completion, error marks, structure view and compiling
   from the IDE keep working without one.

2. One licence per machine. A licence is issued for the station code a designer shows on one
   installation and is valid on that machine only. A second machine needs its own licence.

3. One major version. A licence states the major version it is valid for (for example
   "Valid: 2.x") and covers every release of that major version, including updates of the plugin
   and of the IDE. A new major version requires a new licence.

4. Redistributable Components (Section 3). Applications built with the designers may contain, and
   be distributed with, the tsb.mobile backends, tsbWEB and tsbswing — royalty-free, as part of the
   application and not separately. The forms and source files the designers write belong to the
   Licensee.

